  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 134 PM MDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nFor Thursday, anticipate it will be somewhat drier over the region \nand storms this day will be more confined to the higher terrain, \nwith more isolated activity plains. Additionally, temps will start \nto be on the increase once again.\n\nFriday, a much more pronounced short wave will be moving down in the \nNW flow aloft and winds throughout the column will be rather strong \nas a jet streak will clearly be over the region. The mtns appear \ndrier this day so less convection over the higher terrain, but we may \nsee some organized severe storms over the eastern plains on this day.\n\nWeekend into Monday...Hot. Any storms will be isolated and mainly \nconfined to the mtns. \n\nTuesday we may see cooler weather move in with a better chance of \nprecip. \\/Hodanish",
